---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { withBase, site } from '../../lib/site';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="About"
  description="Yaya Etiabi's academic background, research trajectory, teaching, mentorship and contributions to the research community."
>
  <section class="page-hero">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="eyebrow">Background &amp; academic activities</div>
      <h1>About me</h1>
      <p class="lead">
        I am a machine learning researcher with a PhD in Computer Science and an engineering background
        in embedded systems and telecommunications. My work connects machine learning with wireless
        communications, from collaborative localization to sensing and inference at the network edge.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="container page-content">
    <div class="detail-grid">
      <article class="prose">
        <h2>Research background</h2>
        <p>
          I trained in electrical engineering at Hassan II University, specializing in embedded systems
          and telecommunications. My early research focused on distributed localization in Internet of
          Things (IoT) networks, including robust position estimation from radio measurements.
        </p>
        <p>
          I completed my PhD in Computer Science at Mohammed VI Polytechnic University (UM6P) in 2025.
          My doctoral research investigated collaborative and privacy-preserving machine learning for
          wireless localization. I developed and evaluated federated learning, meta-learning and
          federated distillation methods to address adaptation across indoor environments and the
          communication overhead of distributed training. This research also included a research
          internship at ISEP in Paris.
        </p>
        <p>
          During my postdoctoral appointment at Université du Québec à Montréal (UQAM) in 2025–2026,
          I expanded my work toward AI-native wireless systems and Edge Intelligence. My current research
          interests include integrated sensing, communication and computation (ISCC) for learning and
          inference, as well as radio sensing and localization using multipath measurements.
          The <a href={withBase('/research/')}>Research</a> and
          <a href={withBase('/projects/')}>Projects</a> pages describe these directions and their
          associated studies.
        </p>

        <h2>Research practice</h2>
        <p>
          My research experience covers problem formulation, the design and implementation of learning
          and estimation methods, and experimental evaluation. I work with wireless-system simulations
          and experimental datasets, compare approaches against established baselines, and analyze
          localization accuracy, model adaptation, communication overhead or computational cost,
          depending on the problem. My published work is listed on the
          <a href={withBase('/publications/')}>Publications page</a>.
        </p>

        <h2>Teaching, mentoring and academic service</h2>
        <p>
          I have taught programming and machine learning through laboratory sessions, regular classes
          and hands-on AI training. I have also mentored and supervised undergraduate and master's-level
          research projects, supporting students in developing research questions, implementing methods
          and evaluating their results. Some of this supervised work has contributed to IEEE conference
          publications.
        </p>
        <p>
          My academic service includes membership of the Technical Program Committee for IEEE WCNC 2024
          and peer review for IEEE conferences and journals. Further details of these activities are
          available on the <a href={withBase('/teaching-outreach/')}>Teaching &amp; Outreach page</a>.
        </p>

        <h2>Scientific communication and community involvement</h2>
        <p>
          I have presented my research at international conferences and at academic events. I was a
          finalist in the IEEE ComSoc Three Minute Thesis competition at IEEE ICC 2023, received
          the Best Oral Presenter award at UM6P Doctoral Days, and received the Best Poster
          Presentation award at a MOMI research event hosted by Inria, Université Côte d'Azur.
          These presentations and distinctions are documented on my
          <a href={withBase('/talks/')}>Talks &amp; Presentations page</a>.
        </p>
        <p>
          I also contribute to AI education and knowledge sharing through community classes, webinars
          and public panels. This involvement includes facilitating and mentoring within Black in AI's
          Emerging Leaders in AI program, as well as serving as Director of Scientific and Thematic
          Content at AURA Association.
        </p>
      </article>

      <aside class="sidebar-panel" aria-label="Explore profile and related work">
        <h3>Explore my work</h3>
        <p class="small"><a href={withBase('/research/')}>Research directions ↗</a></p>
        <p class="small"><a href={withBase('/projects/')}>Research projects ↗</a></p>
        <p class="small"><a href={withBase('/publications/')}>Publications ↗</a></p>
        <p class="small"><a href={withBase('/talks/')}>Talks &amp; Presentations ↗</a></p>
        <p class="small"><a href={withBase('/teaching-outreach/')}>Teaching &amp; Outreach ↗</a></p>
        <div class="sidebar-divider" aria-hidden="true"></div>
        <h3>Academic profiles</h3>
        <p class="small"><a href={site.scholar} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google Scholar ↗</a></p>
        <p class="small"><a href={site.orcid} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">ORCID ↗</a></p>
        <p class="small"><a href={site.github} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">GitHub ↗</a></p>
        <p class="small"><a href={site.linkedin} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">LinkedIn ↗</a></p>
        <p class="small"><a href={withBase('/contact/')}>Contact ↗</a></p>
      </aside>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
